blink-aur
========

Arch Linux (AUR) package for blink-qt, a fully featured SIP client with a
Qt based UI.

Files
-----

 * PKGBUILD              - Arch package recipe (use with makepkg/yay)
 * blink.desktop         - desktop entry for the package
 * install.sh            - end-to-end install script (all deps + blink-qt)
 * fix_ffmpeg_pix_fmts.patch - PJSIP 2.10 / FFmpeg 5.1+ compatibility patch

Quick install
-------------

The install script handles the full dependency chain in the correct order:

    ./install.sh

This installs:
  1. Official repo dependencies (pacman)
  2. AUR-only dependencies (yay)
  3. python-sipsimple (built from source with the FFmpeg patch)
  4. blink-qt (built from the PKGBUILD)

Manual build
------------

If all dependencies are already installed:

    makepkg -si

SIP SIMPLE SDK
--------------

The AUR `python-sipsimple` package fails to build against modern FFmpeg
(>= 5.1) because the bundled PJSIP 2.10 uses AVCodec fields (`pix_fmts`,
`supported_framerates`) that were removed.  The `install.sh` script builds
sipsimple from source with `fix_ffmpeg_pix_fmts.patch` applied, which
switches to `avcodec_get_supported_config()`.
